      "note": "ReTraceQA is a 2,421-instance expert-annotated benchmark showing that small language models (SLMs) reach the correct final answer via a flawed reasoning trace 14-24% of the time on commonsense QA, and that LLM-as-judge and PRM evaluators reliably detect overall trace correctness but struggle to localize the specific erroneous step, inflating answer-only accuracy scores by up to 25%.",
